      "message": "I think it\u0027s not an overkill. IMO the mutex/atomic variable(haven\u0027t analyzed if it\u0027s sufficient or not) is needed. I can see a case when the `deactivation_handler` is interrupted (please keep in mind that the work is executed by a different, dedicated thread) at line 28 (before setting gpio, after if), then the `activate` is called (`k_work_cancel_delayable` won\u0027t stop already started work), which sets the GPIO and `is_active \u003d true`, then `deactivation_handler` is finished, which sets the GPIO to 0, which is not an expected result.",
